<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="C_codes">C codes</span></h3>
<ul><li>go into the c directory.</li></ul>
<pre>cd ~/UV-Sensor-code/Pico/c/
</pre>
<ul><li>Add the path of SDK.</li></ul>
<pre>export PICO_SDK_PATH=../../pico-sdk
</pre>
<dl><dd>Note that if the path of your SDK is different, you need to modify the command and use the correct path to export.</dd></dl>
<ul><li>Generate Makefile and build.</li></ul>
<pre>cmake ..
make -j9
</pre>
<ul><li>After building, a uf2 file is generated.</li>
<li>Press and hold the button of Pico, connect it to Raspberry Pi then release the button.</li>
<li>Copy/Drag the uf2 file to the portable disk (RPI-RP2) recognized.</li></ul>
<pre>cp main.uf2 /media/pi/RPI-RP2/
</pre>
